  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **CutMix Augmentation** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cv_cutmix(image_a: list, image_b: list, bbox: list) -> dict:\n    A, B = np.array(image_a, dtype=np.float64), np.array(image_b, dtype=np.float64)\n    H, W = A.shape\n    x1, y1, x2, y2 = [int(v) for v in bbox]\n    mixed = A.copy(); mixed[y1:y2, x1:x2] = B[y1:y2, x1:x2]\n    lam = 1.0 - (float((x2 - x1) * (y2 - y1)) / float(H * W))\n    return {'mixed_image': np.round(mixed, 4).tolist(), 'lambda_label': round(lam, 4)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
